Sample message import file
00-0000 A Thrilling Moment (Johannesburg)
1 One of the most thrilling moments of my life has come. I have waited fifteen years for this opportunity. Ever since I left you, I have wanted with all my heart to see you again. I have prayed very much to come here again.
2 But I firmly believe that with the help of God I will again minister in the Name of the Lord Jesus among the Africans. God has promised to give us the desire of our heart, and this is one of the desires of my heart.
3 In a few minutes I hope to meet you here, to shake your hand and to fellowship together again. I am thankful for all these wonderful people.

Second sample message — no city in the header
00-0001 Answer to Prayer Requests
1 We have received your prayer request and we are happy that you are a believer, and we want to assure you that the Lord heals every sickness. Your request received the personal attention of Brother Branham, and he prayed a special prayer for you over a cloth, according to Acts 19:11-12.
2 We ask that you wear a piece of this cloth next to your heart and believe that God will heal your body. Please wear it and stand firmly on the Word and promise of God. Be simple. Be natural. Keep your heart open before God.
3 We must not be occupied only with our feelings or symptoms, our faith or lack of faith; we must follow only what God has said. The simplest way is to begin to call what we have prayed for OURS and to thank the Lord for it.

Third sample message
00-0002 Wedding Ceremony (Jeffersonville)
1 Dearly beloved, we are gathered here before God and this congregation to join this man and this woman in the holy bonds of matrimony, which Saint Paul commanded to be honorable among all men.
2 Therefore, no one should enter into it unadvisedly or lightly, but soberly, discreetly and in the fear of God.
3 These two persons have come here to be joined in holy marriage. If anyone present can show just cause why they may not be lawfully joined together, let him speak now or forever hold his peace.
